<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end up, seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end up, seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed higher on Sunday but are likely to fall as cotton rates came off after the government relief package for the textile sector cut import duties on cotton and synthetic fibres.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Shafiq (Gold ky)	   465	    460</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 490	    485</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 480	    470</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
